WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Start with a simple idea
Python follows instructions you write. Use print() to display a message. Text inside quotation marks is called a string.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Read the result
Python evaluates the expression inside print(), then displays its value. Adding two numbers produces a number.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Text and numbers behave differently
Quotes matter. The first statement adds numbers. The second displays a string exactly as written.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Ready to practice?
Exercise 1 asks you to recognize print() and evaluate a simple addition. Remember: parentheses hold the value and quotation marks identify text.
